<section class="av_toggle_section av-m8ds4w83-8c2a124faf1d1d778a0b5e72f24e8082" itemprop="mainEntity" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"><div class="single_toggle" data-tags="{All} " role="tablist"><p aria-controls="toggle-id-3" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Click to expand: How is TheraLight 360 therapy administered, and what can I expect during a session?" class="toggler av-title-above" data-aria_collapsed="Click to expand: How is TheraLight 360 therapy administered, and what can I expect during a session?" data-aria_expanded="Click to collapse: How is TheraLight 360 therapy administered, and what can I expect during a session?" data-fake-id="#toggle-id-3" data-slide-speed="200" data-title="How is TheraLight 360 therapy administered, and what can I expect during a session?" data-title-open="" id="toggle-toggle-id-3" itemprop="name" role="tab" tabindex="0">How is TheraLight 360 therapy administered, and what can I expect during a session?<span class="toggle_icon"><span class="vert_icon"></span><span class="hor_icon"></span></span></p><div aria-hidden="true" aria-labelledby="toggle-toggle-id-3" class="toggle_wrap av-title-above" id="toggle-id-3" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer" role="region" tabindex="-1"><div class="toggle_content invers-color" itemprop="text"><p>During a TheraLight 360 session, you will lie comfortably in the full-body light therapy bed. The device emits red and near-infrared light, enveloping your body. Each session typically lasts between 10 to 20 minutes, during which you may experience a gentle warming sensation as circulation increases. The treatment is relaxing and painless, with no downtime required afterward.</p>
